    "lawCode": "Amd §23, Town L; amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Town Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3613\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the town law, in relation to the position of building\ninspector/code enforcement in the town of Windsor\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nProvides that the building inspector/code enforcement is not required\nto reside within the town of Windsor.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSection 1. Section 23 of the town law is amended by adding a new\nsubdivision 23 to read as follows:\n\n23. Notwithstanding the provisions of subdivision one of this section,\nin the town of Windsor, in the county of Broome, the person holding\nthe position of building inspector/code enforcement need not be an\nelector of such town. Provided, however, the person holding the\nposition of building inspector/code enforcement in any other town\nshall be an elector of such town, unless otherwise provided by law.\n\n§ 2. Establishes the effective date.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\nProvides that the building inspector/code enforcement is required to\nreside within the town of Windsor.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nCurrently, the position of building inspector/code enforcement for the\ntown of Windsor is one that requires the holder of that position must\nbe a resident of the town of Windsor. The requirement of Section 23 of\nthe Town Law makes it very difficult for the small town such as\nWindsor to hire an individual with skills; knowledge, experience and\nwho meets the requirements if they are only allowed to look within\ntheir town. This bill would allow the town to look in a broader\nspectrum for the right person for the job.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nTo be determined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
